I§P1 0 J1 {Ptot/N}
Rjc1 CASE1 J1 {Rjc}
Rcs1 SINK CASE1 {Rcs}
I§P2 0 J2 {if(N>=2,Ptot/N,0)}
Rjc2 CASE2 J2 {Rjc}
Rcs2 SINK CASE2 {Rcs}
I§P3 0 J3 {if(N>=3,Ptot/N,0)}
Rjc3 CASE3 J3 {Rjc}
Rcs3 SINK CASE3 {Rcs}
I§P4 0 J4 {if(N>=4,Ptot/N,0)}
Rjc4 CASE4 J4 {Rjc}
Rcs4 SINK CASE4 {Rcs}
Rsa SINK TAMB {Rsa}
Csa SINK TAMB {Csa}
Vamb TAMB 0 {Ta}
* FET 1
* FET 2
* FET 3
* FET 4
* THERMAL MODEL - 150 W into N MOSFETs on the scrap heatsink
* Electrical analogue: 1 V = 1 degC, 1 A = 1 W, 1 ohm = 1 K/W, 1 F = 1 J/K.  V(Jn) = junction temperature.\nPer-FET current loops force equal current, and all drains see the same Vds, so power splits equally.\nRjc = 0.70 K/W (IRFP250N max).  Rcs = 0.5 K/W (TO-247 on a silicone/Kapton insulator + paste; 0.24 bare + grease).\nRsa: heatsink ~ 17 x 9 x 7 cm extruded audio-amp sink: ~0.9 K/W natural convection, ~0.25-0.35 K/W with a\n80-92 mm fan.  ESTIMATE ONLY - measure it (README, "heatsink characterisation").  Csa = 500 J/K ~ 0.55 kg Al.
.param Ptot=150 N=4 Ta=30 Rjc=0.7 Rcs=0.5 Rsa=0.35 Csa=500
.step param N list 2 3 4
.step param Rsa list 0.25 0.35 0.5 0.9
.tran 0 3600 0 2 startup
.ic V(SINK)={Ta}
.meas TRAN Tj_1h FIND V(J1) AT 3600
.meas TRAN Tsink_1h FIND V(SINK) AT 3600
.meas TRAN Tcase_1h FIND V(CASE1) AT 3600
.meas TRAN t_sink_90pct_s WHEN V(SINK)=Ta+0.9*Ptot*Rsa
* PASS: Tj <= 125 degC (50 degC margin to the 175 degC rating, which also keeps the derated DC SOA healthy).
.backanno
.end
